import BoltProof.Bridge.Glue.SimpleMulti.Weld

/-!
# The gate stack's items

The rebuild regions read the stack under the gate flag (`gateT`, suffix 1425) by depth. These lemmas name the
items the refinement needs: the spend's own fields and constants the first rebuild reuses (the new token's
lock-length varint, the pay-to-proof template, the scriptCode's issuer push and suffix, the value, the
grandparent and balance fields, the fifth interop slot) and the two piece sets, item `62 + j` being `psA.p j`
and item `137 + j` being `psB.p j`. All hold by `rfl` for each next type, except the merge flag (item 2, empty off a merge) and the
varint (item 0), which needs the spent lock's widths. Generated by the glue's `gen_gate.py`.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option linter.unusedSimpArgs false

namespace BoltProof.Glue.SimpleMulti

open BsvScript BsvScript.Numbers
open BoltProof.Bridge.Generated
open BoltProof.Glue.MinSimple (sc scLen)

